{% set k = snapshot.keyring %}
<h3>Master key rotation</h3>
<p>Rotation is a command-line operation; this page never edits the keyring or rotates keys. Current state:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Active version {{ k.active_version }}; loaded versions: {{ k.loaded_versions | join(", ") }}</li>
  <li>Rows not yet on the active version: {{ k.stale_rows }}</li>
  <li>Versions referenced by stored keys but missing from the keyring: {{ k.missing_versions | join(", ") or "none" }}</li>
</ul>
<p>Run these on the dashboard host as root (full procedure: <code>docs/operations.md</code>, section 6). Take a database backup first.</p>
<ol>
  <li>Generate the next version into a <strong>new</strong> file in a temporary <code>0700</code> directory owned by the container user, merging the current keyring (live limit: two versions). The current <code>master_key</code> is mounted read-only at <code>/secrets</code> and the new file is written to <code>/out</code>; both paths exist only inside this one <code>docker run</code>:
    <pre><code>set -eu
tmp="$(mktemp -d /tmp/cert-dashboard-keyring.XXXXXXXX)"
install -d -m 0700 -o 10001 -g 10001 "$tmp"
docker run --rm -v /etc/cert-dashboard/secrets:/secrets:ro -v "$tmp":/out cert-dashboard:local \
  python -m app.cli generate-master-key --version {{ next_version }} --merge /secrets/master_key --output /out/master_key.v{{ next_version }}.new
sha256sum "$tmp/master_key.v{{ next_version }}.new"</code></pre>
    The command prints only <code>sha256=&lt;digest&gt; path=&lt;file&gt;</code>; the digest must equal the <code>sha256sum</code> output.</li>
  <li>Keep a copy of the old file in the backup location, install the verified file as the <code>master_key</code> secret and restart so new writes use it:
    <pre><code>install -m 0400 -o 10001 -g 10001 "$tmp/master_key.v{{ next_version }}.new" /etc/cert-dashboard/secrets/master_key
shred -u -- "$tmp/master_key.v{{ next_version }}.new" &amp;&amp; rmdir -- "$tmp"
docker compose up -d --force-recreate web worker</code></pre></li>
  <li>Re-encrypt every key and TOTP seed (batched, idempotent, resumable):
    <pre><code>docker compose run --rm web python -m app.cli rotate-master-key</code></pre></li>
  <li>Verify a keyed certificate (metadata only is printed):
    <pre><code>docker compose run --rm web python -m app.cli verify-key --certificate-id ID</code></pre></li>
</ol>
<p class="hint">Secret files are read once at startup: replace the file, rerun <code>scripts/install-secrets.sh</code> and restart the service.</p>
<h3>Prune old jobs</h3>
<p>Queues the retention cleanup now: finished jobs older than the retention period, old scan results, expired sessions and old artifacts are removed. Audit rows are never removed.</p>
<form method="post" action="/settings/maintenance/prune">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
  <label for="f-prune-confirm">Type {{ prune_confirmation }} to confirm</label>
  <input id="f-prune-confirm" name="confirm" autocomplete="off" required>
  <button type="submit" class="button-destructive">Queue retention cleanup</button>
</form>
